# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WeatherGPT — configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in the values you have. Every setting is
# OPTIONAL: with none of them the app still runs completely, because all
# weather, air-quality and climate endpoints are keyless and query
# understanding falls back to the local deterministic parser.
#
# Each key simply upgrades one capability:
#   Gemini   → answers open-ended questions the rule parser cannot classify
#   Sarvam   → accurate Indian-language speech in and out
#   Deepgram → higher-quality English speech synthesis
#
# ⚠️  SECURITY: Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the client bundle, so
# these keys are readable by anyone who loads the page. Fine for local
# development and demos; before deploying publicly, move these calls behind the
# API gateway sketched in the README so credentials stay on the server.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Google AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey) ------------------
# Powers Tier 2: tool-calling for compound and unanticipated questions.
# Keys look like "AIza...". Pin the model — availability varies by project, and
# some newer IDs ignore JSON response mode.
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=
VITE_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# --- Sarvam AI (https://dashboard.sarvam.ai) --------------------------------
# Speech recognition (saarika) and synthesis (bulbul) for Indian languages,
# markedly better than the browser's built-in engine for Hindi, Bengali,
# Tamil, Telugu, Marathi, Gujarati, Kannada, Malayalam and Punjabi.
VITE_SARVAM_API_KEY=

# --- Deepgram (https://console.deepgram.com) -------------------------------
# English speech synthesis (aura-2). Indian languages route to Sarvam instead.
VITE_DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=

# --- Clerk (https://dashboard.clerk.com) -----------------------------------
# Optional sign-in. Without it the app runs exactly as before and saved places
# live in this browser; with it, saved places and preferences follow the user to
# any device.
#
# Publishable keys are designed to be public, so this one legitimately belongs in
# the client bundle. The CLERK_SECRET_KEY is NOT — nothing here needs it, because
# every Clerk call from the browser is authenticated by the user's session.
# Never add it with a VITE_ prefix.
#
# Get a key: create an application at dashboard.clerk.com, or run
#   npx clerk@latest auth login && npx clerk@latest init
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
